Native Plan 9 time delta for QuickJS 2026-06-04 (generated9 port)
================================================================

generated9's quickjs.c has:

    #if defined(_WIN32) || defined(PLAN9)
        ... struct tm *tm; gmtime(); mktime(); ...

That fallback was written for APE, which provides POSIX struct tm and
localtime_r.  Native Plan 9 does not: libc.h exposes Tm *gmtime(long) and
Tm *localtime(long), so declaring struct-tm gmtime/mktime would collide.

This scaffold's p9time.c supplies localtime_r()/gmtime_r() and a struct tm
with tm_gmtoff.  The engine therefore uses the POSIX branch instead:

    -#if defined(_WIN32) || defined(PLAN9)
    +#if defined(_WIN32)

Apply after vendoring from generated9:

    sed 's/#if defined(_WIN32) || defined(PLAN9)/#if defined(_WIN32)/' \
        quickjs.c > quickjs.c.new
    mv quickjs.c.new quickjs.c

vendor.rc does this automatically and refuses to run unless the input has
exactly one matching line.  No other generated9 PLAN9 source delta is
changed by this scaffold.
